    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_284a1859",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: this_man_took_millions_of_lives; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts Adolf Hitler, a historical figure responsible for the Holocaust and the deaths of millions, with the text 'this man took millions of lives.' The overall intent is to convey a stark, unambiguous condemnation of Hitler's atrocities. While the message is factually accurate and serves an educational or moral purpose, it is inherently harmful because it reifies the historical trauma associated with Hitler and the Nazi regime. The meme's intent is not to threaten or abuse, but to shock and warn viewers about the consequences of extreme ideologies and totalitarianism. The juxtaposition of the image of Hitler with the text serves as a direct, visceral reminder of the human cost of his actions, functioning as a form of historical propaganda aimed at preventing the recurrence of such atrocities. The meme does not target any specific individual or group based on protected characteristics, but its content is deeply tied to the historical trauma of genocide and war, making it potentially triggering and emotionally charged for survivors and descendants of victims.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_37a6d23c"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
