      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_b433e2cf",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "Adolf_Hitler",
      "label": "Adolf Hitler",
      "description": "The German chancellor and dictator of Nazi Germany from 1933 until his death in 1945. He is the central historical figure referenced in the meme. The image of Hitler is iconic and universally recognized as the leader responsible for the Holocaust and World War II. The meme's message is only comprehensible because of the global historical knowledge of Hitler's identity and his role in orchestrating mass murder.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_37a6d23c"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_f751389b",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "Anti_Semitism",
      "label": "Anti-Semitism",
      "description": "A long-standing prejudice and discrimination against Jewish people, which was institutionalized and radicalized by the Nazi regime. The Holocaust was the culmination of centuries of anti-Semitic hatred. The meme's condemnation of Hitler implicitly references his promotion of anti-Semitic ideology as the core driver of his genocidal policies, which is a key piece of background knowledge for understanding the historical context.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_37a6d23c"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_d4d210bc",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "Genocide",
      "label": "Genocide",
      "description": "The deliberate and systematic destruction of a racial, political, or cultural group. The Holocaust is the most infamous example of genocide in history. The meme's text 'this man took millions of lives' is only meaningful because it refers to the concept of genocide, which is a specific, legally and morally defined term that requires external knowledge to understand the scale and nature of the atrocity.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
